Part (a): Derive the following Thermodynamic Functions and Heat Capacity from the Partition Function relation from the preceding result, showing the algebra, calculus, counting, or physical identity used at each step.
\[
\frac{\partial U}{\partial\beta}
=\frac{\partial}{\partial\beta}
\left(\frac{\sum_rE_re^{-\beta E_r}}{Z_N}\right)
=-\frac{\sum_rE_r^2e^{-\beta E_r}}{Z_N}
+\frac{\left(\sum_rE_re^{-\beta E_r}\right)^2}{Z_N^2}
=-\langle E^2\rangle+\langle E\rangle^2,
\qquad
\frac{d\beta}{dT}=-\frac{1}{k_{\mathrm B}T^2}.
\tag*{[4]}
\]

Part (b): Reconstruct the complete mathematical chain for Thermodynamic Functions and Heat Capacity from the Partition Function, from the starting relation to the final result. Include every required substitution, derivative, integral, or limiting step.
Start:
\[
Z_N=\sum_r e^{-\beta E_r},
\qquad
p_r=\frac{e^{-\beta E_r}}{Z_N}.
\tag*{[1]}
\]

Target:
\[
C_{V,\mathrm{tot}}=\left(\frac{\partial U}{\partial T}\right)_{V,N}
=\frac{\langle E^2\rangle-\langle E\rangle^2}{k_{\mathrm B}T^2}
=k_{\mathrm B}\beta^2\left(\langle E^2\rangle-\langle E\rangle^2\right)\ge0.
\tag*{[5]}
\]

